{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966793,"nonce":"tNAboh9MHg3J3RO89DV4O9LA5Yg=","title":"Glyph rasterisation followed the post-transform size with no floor — at canvas zoom 0.1 a","message":"`GpuPaintContext::draw_text` in blinc_gpu/src/paint.rs multiplied\n`style.size` by `current_uniform_scale()` (sqrt(|det|) of the active\naffine) and passed the result straight into swash. At canvas zoom\n0.1 a 12px label asked for a 1.2px raster; swash returned near-empty\nhinted bitmaps, the atlas size-quantiser\n(`(font_size*2.0).round() as u16` in blinc_text/src/atlas.rs) merged\nseveral nearby sub-pixel sizes into one bucket, and the SDF shader's\n`pow(coverage, 0.7)` crushed already-faint alpha (pow(0.1, 0.7)=0.20).\nAtlas sampler was Nearest min/mag/mipmap (text.rs:73-75) so no LOD\nfallback.\n\nFor a canvas-based UI / vector editor — node-editor included — this\nmade text DISAPPEAR at high zoom-out. Capping `min_zoom` would\nhave been a workaround, not a fix; the user explicitly rejected\nthat since high zoom-out range is a hard requirement.\n\n**Fix shipped 2026-06-19** (raster CLAMP — floor AND ceiling):\n- `paint::draw_text`: introduce\n  `TEXT_RASTER_FLOOR = 6.0` and `TEXT_RASTER_CEILING = 48.0`.\n  Compute `raster_size = scaled_size.clamp(FLOOR, CEILING)` and\n  `quad_scale = scaled_size / raster_size`. Pass `raster_size`\n  (not `scaled_size`) into `prepare_text_with_style` so swash\n  rasterises at a legible size that ALSO doesn't grow a new atlas\n  bucket per zoom step. After receiving the laid-out glyphs,\n  scale each glyph's bounds rect (offset-from-origin + w/h) by\n  `quad_scale` so the on-screen quad covers the intended\n  display footprint. UV bounds in `gradient_params` point at the\n  clamped atlas tile and are unchanged.\n- `text.rs`: glyph atlas sampler's `min_filter` AND `mag_filter`\n  switched from Nearest to Linear (mipmap stays Nearest since\n  we have a single mip). Linear minification handles zoom-out\n  below the floor; Linear magnification handles zoom-in above\n  the ceiling. Crispness at exact 1:1 stays effectively\n  pixel-perfect because the raster size matches the display\n  size — UV centres line up with atlas texel centres.\n\n**Why the ceiling matters more than the floor in practice**: at\ndeep zoom-in, swash rasterises bigger and bigger glyphs as the\ndisplay size grows. Each unique scaled size creates a new atlas\nbucket via the `(font_size*2.0).round()` quantiser. The atlas\nre-rasterises EVERY visible glyph at the new size each frame the\nzoom moves — that's the \"lag worsens as I zoom in deeper,\npersists when I zoom back out\" symptom. The ceiling caps atlas\ngrowth: above 48px raster, the same atlas tile is reused and the\nquad scales up. Atlas pressure is now bounded by the *count* of\nunique glyphs on screen, not the zoom level.\n\nTogether: a 1.2px display-size text renders by painting a 6px\nswash bitmap into a 1.2px quad and sampling it min-filtered.\nGlyph stays visible from 0.05x to ~10x zoom; at deep zoom-in the\nmag_filter=Nearest path stays pixel-perfect.\n\n**Proper architectural fix (deferred — larger work)**: a true\nSDF/MSDF text pipeline. Rasterise each glyph once into a distance\nfield atlas at 32-64px reference, add an `is_msdf` flag bit to\nPRIM_TEXT's `flags`, add an MSDF branch in the shader that does\n`smoothstep(0.5 - fwidth(d), 0.5 + fwidth(d), median(msdf.rgb))`.\nReplaces the `pow(coverage, 0.7)` gamma trick and the size-bucket\ndedup with a single high-quality raster that's sharp from 0.05x\nto 50x without quad scaling. Best built as its own pipeline\noutside the sdf_core megaswitch to avoid the uniformity-rule\nproblems flagged in shaders.rs around the existing PRIM_TEXT case.\nSee workflow output at\n`/private/tmp/.../tasks/w164i1bau.output` for the full design.\n\n**Risks worth watching**:\n- Linear `min_filter` requires the atlas's free regions to be\n  cleared to 0, not garbage. `GlyphAtlas::grow` at\n  blinc_text/src/atlas.rs around line 259 — verify new rows are\n  zeroed; if not, minified samples may bleed neighbouring glyphs\n  on the first frame after an atlas grow.\n- The size-bucket clustering around the new 6px floor could\n  trigger evict-churn for the band 0.5px-6px display sizes that\n  used to spread across multiple buckets. Should be a net cache\n  WIN (fewer buckets means fewer atlas entries) but worth\n  measuring on a label-heavy scene.\n- The `quad_scale` write touches `glyph.bounds[0..4]` after\n  layout. If a downstream consumer of `PositionedGlyph` reads\n  the bounds for a different purpose (hit-testing, selection\n  rects), it would see the scaled-down bounds — fine for\n  display but might surprise selection logic. Today only\n  `GpuPrimitive::from_glyph` consumes these bounds so the\n  change is contained.","files":null}]}